# Agent git hygiene (neop)

**Default:** topic branch on the **primary clone** (`/Users/andrew/workspace/neop` or this checkout’s main tree). Do **not** create `neop-wt/*` worktrees for ordinary feature / PR work.

Same posture as Alliance HQ: isolate with **branches** first. See also the user rule **Agent git hygiene (branches first)** / `~/.cursor/rules/agent-git-hygiene.mdc`.

## Prefer primary + branches

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| `git checkout -b feat/<topic>` on primary | Default to `git worktree add ../neop-wt/...` |
| One agent → one branch → one PR concern | Two agents on the same branch |
| Stop/ask if primary is dirty or another agent owns it | Silent worktree to dodge WIP |

**Worktree only when:** maintainer asks; primary is actively used by another writer; concurrent implementing agents need two trees; or **Real Steel** overlay/skill requires a dedicated worktree.

## Real Steel exception

`/real-steel` on neop may use a dedicated worktree when the Real Steel skill/overlay says so (then `move_agent_to_root` once into that tree). Otherwise prefer the PR branch on primary. Parent must not edit primary while a Real Steel worktree is the active writer.

## Anon + identity

Before commit/push/`gh` writes: local `.identity` with `required_profile=anon`, then `github-identity anon` / `check`. See AGENTS.md and user identity rules. Never commit `.identity`.

## Cleanup

Remove task worktrees when done; delete merged local topic branches; keep primary on `main` when idle.
